# Climatic Mysteries — unpack camera (do not rewrite)

## Why this rule exists

Agents kept replacing the whole camera system each pass. **Tune in place** via `buildItemCameraFocus` unless the owner explicitly asks for a new approach.

## Locked approach (live `app.html`)

**Actual camera focus** — not magnifier-on-a-point:

1. **`object-position`** — pan the cover crop so the item moves toward frame center (stays sharp).
2. **`scale` + `translate`** — center the item on screen, then zoom (`buildItemCameraFocus`).
3. **Pin / flash** — screen center (item should land there).

Do **not** revert to scale-only from `transform-origin` on item percent without the pan step.

**Coordinates:** mask centroids on `rental_unpack_scene.png` (1536×1024). **Scale:** ~2.0–2.15 per item.

| id | x | y | scale |
|----|---|---|-------|
| duffel | 48.8 | 77.1 | 2.05 |
| folder | 62.5 | 78.1 | 2.10 |
| notebook | 50.1 | 84.0 | 2.15 |
| bottle | 37.1 | 76.2 | 2.15 |
| keys | 58.6 | 45.9 | 2.05 |

## Allowed edits

- Change **one** item’s `x`, `y`, or `scale` in `UNPACK_OBJECTS`.
- Or small tweaks inside `buildItemCameraFocus` only when owner reports all edge items wrong on one axis.

**Not allowed** without owner asking: delete `buildItemCameraFocus`, bbox auto-zoom, separate camera systems.

## Workflow

1. Owner says a version works → **git commit** (`cm: unpack camera ok`).
2. Owner names **one item** and direction — not “fix camera again”.
3. Deploy: `bash climaticMysteries/scripts/deploy.sh`.
